{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id319173301"}, "name":{"label":"Madame piccolini"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-06-03T00:15:12-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.81.4"}, "id":{"label":"11337709959"}, "title":{"label":"Not just a tracker, they make you care…"}, "content":{"label":"…about being (and staying) hydrated. \n \nI LOVE that you can track different kinds of beverages and that the developers used (and provide) scientific resources for working out different levels of hydration - or dehydration (for alcoholic drinks).\nThe push notifications are also not your standard “don’t forget to drink something” [especially for many of us with ADHD, who already feel bad about forgetting stuff, this just creates negative feelings towards a task, even if we wanted to do it] …. but Waterllama’s reminders are more along the lines of “Hydration is super important for your kidneys to be happy” or “Hey, good job, only 876ml to meet your goal!”  — so while I can’t really shake the habit of ignoring the reminder itself while being in the middle of something, it helps me get a way more positive attitude towards wanting to stay hydrated - to the point that I didn’t only meet, but even exceeded my hydration goal most days. \n\nI also really like that you can see your streak and the hydration statistics - this helps me stay on track on days like today where I can’t really be bothered to get up and refill my bottle, but then do it so I don’t lose the streak.\n\nI paid for the premium version (thanks for making this a one-off lifetime purchase rather than monthly subscription).", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=1454778585&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
